WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.660
- [Bran] Everything you did brought you

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:04.530
where you are now, where you belong.

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:06.260
- The creators of "Game of Thrones"

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:08.600
have signed a monumental
new deal with Netflix,

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.080
but can they live up to it?

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.390
We'll take a look right now on the new

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:13.570
Rotten Tomatoes show, "The Ketchup".

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:15.650
David Benioff and Dan Weiss are moving on

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:17.470
from HBO and will create and develop

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:19.210
new projects for the streaming giant

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:21.480
after signing a 200 million dollar

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.120
multi-year overall film and TV deal.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.460
It's one of Netflix's biggest deals yet

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.060
and beat out other serious contenders

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:30.040
like Amazon, thought
to be the front runner

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.180
at one time, and Disney, with whom the duo

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.770
already have a deal to write
three "Star Wars" movies.

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.530
Benioff and Weiss, who created and served

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.210
as showrunners on HBO's
mega-hit "Game of Thrones"

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.350
are coming off a polarizing final season

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:44.390
that's a rotten 58% on the Tomato meter.

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:46.330
And even though it did
set a new Emmy record

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:48.500
for the most nominations
by a single program

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.710
in one year with 32, it
kinda makes you wonder

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:53.780
if the season suffered
'cause they were checked out

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:55.740
and already onto other projects,

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.730
and people on Twitter
don't seem that impressed

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:59.890
with Netflix giving
these guys a huge deal,

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:01.797
saying things like, "Benioff and Weiss

00:01:01.797 --> 00:01:03.647
"have unique experience
in running a big budget

00:01:03.647 --> 00:01:05.847
"show with lots of moving
parts, but I just can't

00:01:05.847 --> 00:01:08.177
"see how they're worth
200 million dollars.

00:01:08.177 --> 00:01:09.987
"They're not Ryan Murphy who produces like

00:01:09.987 --> 00:01:11.840
"three original hits a year,"

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:15.007
and "Whispers, Benioff and Weiss were not

00:01:15.007 --> 00:01:17.420
"the reason people liked
'Game of Thrones.'"

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:18.777
Then there's my personal favorite,

00:01:18.777 --> 00:01:20.577
"Perhaps after it's all said and done,

00:01:20.577 --> 00:01:22.537
"the greatest thing Benioff and Weiss ever

00:01:22.537 --> 00:01:24.967
"gave us was the endless Lena Headey

00:01:24.967 --> 00:01:26.817
"as Cersei Lannister gifs to respond to

00:01:26.817 --> 00:01:28.710
"all of their future projects."

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:31.860
- Sometimes I wonder, if this
is the price for our sins.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.690
- As far as what this means for HBO,

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:35.790
it's worth noting that
the two will be credited

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:37.987
as executive producers on any and all

00:01:37.987 --> 00:01:40.510
"Game of Thrones" prequel
series moving forward,

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:42.370
and the upcoming series
"Confederate" which

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:43.780
the duo was set to write and serve

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:46.500
as showrunners on, is now off their books.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.410
No word yet on if the contriversal project

00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:50.680
will move to Netflix as
part of their new deal.

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:52.650
When it comes to "Star
Wars", the first film

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:54.330
in their trilogy has already been slated

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:58.120
for a December 16th 2022
release, with the others

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:00.320
most likely coming every
two years after that.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.410
So when exactly the guys
will find time for new

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:05.400
Netflix projects seems to
be a pretty valid question.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:06.900
- May the force be with you.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.180
- And then there's Netflix.

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:10.390
This deal comes after
a wave of cancellations

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:12.237
for scripted shows like "The OA",

00:02:12.237 --> 00:02:14.550
"She's Gotta Have It",
and "Designated Survivor",

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:16.860
not to mention seminal
female created shows

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.470
like "One Day at a Time",
and "Tuca and Bertie".

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:20.880
But with the streaming
wars just heating up

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.970
you gotta make room for
big moves considering

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:25.220
the company already has
deals with mega-producers

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:27.850
Ryan Murphy, Shonda
Rhimes, and Kenya Barris

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:28.700
among others.

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:31.077
- Whatever stands in our
way, we will defeat it.

00:02:31.077 --> 00:02:32.690
- So, let me turn it over to you.

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.710
- What do you think, do Benioff and Weiss

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:36.360
deserv this big of a deal?

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.160
Did you have issues with the last season

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:40.450
of "Game of Thrones", or
did you secretly love it

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:42.250
and you just are ashamed to admit it?

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:43.330
You can tell us.

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:44.680
Let us know in the comment section,

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.130
and tell us what other stories you'd love

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:47.830
to see us cover, and for all the latest

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:50.910
streaming news head on
over to RottenTomatoes.com.

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:52.390
Thanks for watching our
new show, "The Ketchup",

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:53.800
where we explore what the latest news

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.940
from movies and TV means to you.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:57.903
Until next time, I'm Mark Ellis.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.383
(upbeat music)

